
---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our Story · Our Purpose</div>
      <h1>Protecting the source.<br />Building the future.</h1>
      <p>
        Watercana began with a simple belief: protecting
        natural freshwater springs should not depend
        entirely on donations or external funding.
        Conservation can be built into a sustainable
        commercial enterprise.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/conservation/">
          Discover our conservation model
        </a>
        <a class="btn alt" href="/contact/">
          Join our journey
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">How it began</div>
        <h2>A different approach to protecting water.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Natural springs are valuable freshwater resources,
          yet protecting the environments that sustain them
          is often overlooked.
        </p>
        <p>
          Watercana was founded to explore a practical
          solution: create a commercially viable spring-water
          business that directly contributes to protecting
          its own source.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rather than treating conservation as a separate
          activity, we are making it part of the business
          model from the beginning.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card story-highlight">
        <div class="eyebrow">Our guiding principle</div>
        <h2>Conservation with every sip.</h2>
        <p>
          Every successful step toward commercialisation
          brings us closer to a model where water sales
          support the long-term protection of natural springs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our foundation</div>
      <h2>We started by protecting the source.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Before launching bottled-water operations,
        Watercana secured land adjacent to its first
        natural spring in Belgut, Kenya.
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>01 · Land protection</h3>
          <p>
            Acquiring spring-adjacent land provides a
            foundation for reducing human disturbance
            and protecting the surrounding environment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>02 · Environmental stewardship</h3>
          <p>
            Conservation efforts include restricting
            disruptive human activities and supporting
            indigenous reforestation around the spring.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>03 · Water-quality assessment</h3>
          <p>
            Preliminary laboratory analysis was completed
            in January 2026. The findings are informing
            plans for treatment, further testing and
            responsible commercial production.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our direction</div>
      <h2>Purpose drives our business.</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Our mission</div>
          <h3>Water with responsibility.</h3>
          <p>
            To provide quality spring water through
            responsible commercial practices that protect
            natural springs and support surrounding
            communities.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Our vision</div>
          <h3>Protected for generations.</h3>
          <p>
            A future where natural springs are protected
            for generations through commercially
            sustainable conservation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Our commitment</div>
          <h3>20% of net profits.</h3>
          <p>
            Once the business generates profits, we commit
            20% of net profits to spring conservation,
            indigenous reforestation and community
            environmental awareness.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Where we are today</div>
      <h2>From conservation to commercial readiness.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Watercana is in its pre-launch stage. Our first
        spring has been identified, adjacent land acquired,
        and conservation activities undertaken.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our next priorities are establishing an appropriate
        water-treatment and bottling facility, completing
        additional water-quality verification, meeting
        applicable regulatory requirements, and piloting
        distribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial bottling and product sales have not yet
        commenced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">The bigger picture</div>
      <h2>One spring is only the beginning.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Our ambition extends beyond a single water source.
      </p>
      <p>
        We envision expanding the Watercana model to
        additional natural springs through responsible
        land acquisition or long-term leases, environmental
        restoration and carefully planned water production.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are also exploring refillable water-supply
        solutions for schools and institutions as part
        of our longer-term distribution strategy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Grow with us</div>
      <h2>Help us turn conservation into a lasting business model.</h2>
      <p>
        We welcome conversations with conservation partners,
        technical specialists, institutions and investors
        who share our long-term vision.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href="/contact/">
        Partner with Watercana
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .story-highlight {
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .story-highlight h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .section .wrap > p {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .section .card p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .story-highlight {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
